                  <h3>SVG Tools</h3>=0A<p>You can kinda smell a vibe-coded =
app these days. <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/mqg_bC4C23sAt7=
O7_5wbTA~~/AABEfhA~/n6lbXWFs3cPTJHU36VjRj-EyEKVACHkkdLRSYmXsarnsqWVnUcsiwMw=
cKqzVzo9wrYkgg6r0mYT1D_U5i3Z8YTktpUHNUgQGJhB-h9N5JxXmLHWIZ2z1689t0Dlw7H5Y">=
TypingSVG</a> has that odor, but like=E2=80=A6 in a good way=3F An app like=
 this absolutely <em>should</em> exist. Someone needed it, and how instead =
of it just being some little tool they=E2=80=99ve tucked away for themselve=
s or thrown away, they tossed it up on some inexpensive hosting and now we =
all have it.</p>=0A<p>I give it some text and a variety of options and it p=
roduces an SVG file with a typing animation on it. Like this: <a href=3D"ht=
tps://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/_VzqVXNIAfxGVbmvLivAOQ~~/AABEfhA~/a_ZBqsEvz=
ZnePNvl7UJ0TswApwetL3jWwF3ZDC0VYcgEF8QkSmHdsH4dXoy5AI19RWM24Rj75QbVyq4_DyKA=
-yorpxxkwCLl5b_MktbZLeTvpD2Vh5d6G7kjcbMiJVaPva1oNO-ADZYecWm0xKBXeo8uO8tbKPn=
goeF2qV2id5o~">view GIF</a></p>=0A<p><a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.c=
om/f/a/_VzqVXNIAfxGVbmvLivAOQ~~/AABEfhA~/a_ZBqsEvzZnePNvl7UJ0TswApwetL3jWwF=
3ZDC0VYcgEF8QkSmHdsH4dXoy5AI19RWM24Rj75QbVyq4_DyKA-yorpxxkwCLl5b_MktbZLeTvp=
D2Vh5d6G7kjcbMiJVaPva1oNO-ADZYecWm0xKBXeo8uO8tbKPngoeF2qV2id5o~">This anima=
ted SVG</a> will work even as an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code>, which might be n=
ews to some. They=E2=80=99ll let you hotlink the image (so it works with qu=
ery params, essentially), but I=E2=80=99ve uploaded it to our own site for =
longevity.</p>=0A<p>Why does it look vibe-coded=3F Involvement of purple. V=
ercel subdomain. Random dark mode for no particular reason. Very simple com=
ponentry with box shadows around everything. I suspect this look will just =
be a funny blip in time, as I=E2=80=99m already noticing a new fancier aest=
hetic emerge from Claude Code that uses their <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpo=
stmail2.com/f/a/WsjLyj-mMu3ff0rY4N-6-Q~~/AABEfhA~/VUynnl20kOAo9pwApNoWUIlkw=
Nx6mMzx3hSdTSKaj7iXZYJJJQlMJI7nIxAeIMlIDTRS3F1LeFzDyCfSo5dihe8U4nxBEdpdf3no=
sjDreu9DEfVKqFDOmkRUpT31C8CNF20CZsEBTUy6WgDkZ8-47ECHutDDeshNlFvLW_hp3zc~">F=
ront-end Design Skill</a> that involves kinda classy all-caps headers and f=
ooters with more exotic font choices.</p>=0A<hr />=0A<p>OK I guess we=E2=80=
=99re doing SVG now, so here we go.</p>=0A<p>I don=E2=80=99t know if <a hre=
f=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/SezQu28d6I_qkNkrfbFIfQ~~/AABEfhA~/T3=
3DFK9hsLUBUgNLf5C-smetMANROMp2CVWIbUBLXrb8-nMHJyblbEi-1pU5KujnmF3tJ8EQQhXmH=
xzkdNnhAtxiGpySIeODOljAuRjwZyiHCdQ-q78Es-iYiOPSumKX">Stroke</a> is vibe-cod=
ed, but maybe! There is one where you draw (kinda begs for a signature), an=
d then it animates where you just drew (drawed=3F).</p>=0A<img src=3D"https=
://production-codepen-email-assets.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D=
600,quality=3D90,format=3Dauto/codepen-spark/stroke_example.png" alt=3D"'Co=
depen' written in digital cursive. " width=3D"450"/>=0A<p>I=E2=80=99m not e=
mbedding this one as animated because it actually gives you a React compone=
nt with a pretty hefty dependency (<a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com=
/f/a/x1g1KM4Dp5DZxGArCT2ZyQ~~/AABEfhA~/n6lbXWFs3cPTJHU36VjRj7gzkELTfpJEuL-A=
ARemr2r1SHarISUejy1Xiy-aK7IupGsNK1wRu7hg4Hs19PI5-eaXl68hUpS0XB8-hW1si0fWNnz=
wqVpYFUZLgs5gcQJp">Motion</a>). It=E2=80=99s a neat tool, but I find that a=
 bummer, as I don=E2=80=99t think React or Motion is required for this to w=
ork, and it would be a lot more usable with some simple built-in styles or =
a web component with props to control it.</p>=0A<hr />=0A<p><a href=3D"http=
s://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/YI9v8cu3GzvWNGwHVg3sDg~~/AABEfhA~/HqVPavBpH8A=
arsKsPU79frItHJqMIEZjT9pJWvtaSxmcqwIMu5ZH3oxXBgSk1rlVZfyKWZOG4vuo1EoLEMlfAc=
gIx1WFwn5obF4yu0GQzdlV1t2P8xdrZRGY3dENrhhW">SVG Doodles</a>: <em>=E2=80=9CB=
rowse a curated collection of free, customizable SVG doodles and icons to u=
se in your websites, apps, slides, and prints.=E2=80=9D</em></p>=0A<img src=
=3D"https://production-codepen-email-assets.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image=
/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=3Dauto/codepen-spark/svg_doodles_demo.png"=
 alt=3D"A sampling of the SVG doodles. " width=3D"450"/>=0A<hr />=0A<p><a h=
ref=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/lf9oFwVnyk0--al6HaVO5w~~/AABEfhA~/=
tiNcny8fiT373D4pppWEnrDdGI7b9fiPhguBJA_DCilR3_Spv_fOEc9Q_CYId3CvaTjUz2YkZBX=
cO9fLlXKNfibB18nzzgAPd87SQm8SkP2XU67VEIuWWmAebSCScCkWhU6vYQekaNyZ-Os4lOh3tq=
Xb6q6oeFkn3eQbnDWDkzY~">You can <em>almost</em> use the straight-up SVG syn=
tax</a> directly in CSS (like as a background-image), which is very satisfy=
ing. You do have to URL encode a handful of characters. You aren=E2=80=99t =
gonna get syntax highlighting though. I=E2=80=99d have a stronger urge for =
CSS to make this even nicer, but <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f=
/a/-djmLLAuDjDq7uxYNWhFlQ~~/AABEfhA~/-3rTcDp43ZapmSSKGUsmST1tyTYfxKSQ1ixb0W=
2f2dbcnI2ziV042F4ss1eTMCyVesFCihvet0PsLbrmu5K_BiODmG6iJfKqTjc3ht1Qlc3kRCmqo=
JQKOBD2PM8rdJZIjHx5Fv-_OnBdIuGicWIC90_T49RseHnytIXK_d_u8vOcURp0JW4PdTPebz2x=
UusOrYIRMuij7GCiJG9VnktqXw~~"><code>shape()</code></a> quells my desires si=
nce it=E2=80=99s so good at doing its own thing. David Bushell has a nice <=
a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/1arl40mrhEFoumTZq9TLNQ~~/AABEfh=
A~/ptH0wAB4jzyfgiWP-2tvYKWLIJtoa7ibihc16UzripbeOni4WnkN9f7RhqKFJOLcvtGubiDb=
uz1HwNnwFskKTgo5-j9Zj48lyZdTy_LIV8FdgNfGMS2AeCiYjyhEoFiXyqkbkutQQnxtIQY4SED=
QM1xQujSJhb3IpduR7aYK3kMczkZMfNFnH1TD2X7OkGMt">SVG Optimization and Accessi=
bility Basics</a> guide.</p>=0A<hr />=0A<p>Poor SVG. It=E2=80=99s old techn=
ology that hardly ever changes, yet for as much as people find new cool use=
s for it, people also still find <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f=
/a/EAzW3OaAp4StYNpSAggWRQ~~/AABEfhA~/qUuSgSgn_rR6nWy7ngagVLtUVdakO2f9m66PTn=
HPVeq-IKcg_P3oEtuuE0sgCYDWh0Y7iYYz-0MLf8qd4VNp38NR498TMHNjUwLx-rTEgWxfRE77_=
E6ggTR9eRRQ__gKKW67YEzT8Yd8C07YC4b2gg~~">security vulnerabilities with it</=
a>. This one is about clickjacking, which is basically half social engineer=
ing, that is, placing stuff on the page that tricks you into interacting wi=
th it.</p>=0A<hr />=0A<p>I=E2=80=99ll leave you with Fotis Papadogeorgopoul=
os=E2=80=99 <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/KGcwpf3sKUZKkocBic=
5fPQ~~/AABEfhA~/ARMI1c0e3gnThlVI2Hsrw0S0tOWdZItcSzI2vabnoSw2v38oQEE2ZNwUWwX=
gOK4gQG4Ql8CHz3FrFN21HfYigolu0ewchd5GdrKsKc7f4goFV0OkGstAvLvpxGr_kbSyQh5upe=
Ogz78fxOX0b1pEBA~~"><code>@svg-use</code></a>, which I haven=E2=80=99t trie=
d yet, but it=E2=80=99s a way to lean into SVG=E2=80=99s <code>&lt;use&gt;<=
/code> element. I can say that there are a ton of pro=E2=80=99s and con=E2=
=80=99s to all the ways to display SVG. I too was enamored with <code>&lt;u=
se&gt;</code> for a while as it seems like it can be so efficient in so man=
y ways. It can be, but the downsides are real, like the lack of stylability=
 and the inability to load from a third-party domain. But this tool is deep=
ly in JavaScript, which I imagine can take a stab at solving both.</p>=0D=
